00:00:07.577 --> 00:00:09.054
&gt;&gt; Chris: NURSING HOMES HAVE

00:00:09.088 --> 00:00:11.047
BORNE THE BRUNT OF THE

00:00:11.082 --> 00:00:12.285
CORONAVIRUS PANDEMIC IN THIS

00:00:12.319 --> 00:00:14.777
COUNTRY AND SOME OF THE SADDEST

00:00:14.778 --> 00:00:16.225
SCENES HAVE BEEN OF SENIORS

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.343
PASSING AWAY WITH THEIR FAMILIES

00:00:18.345 --> 00:00:20.773
UNABLE TO BE ALONGSIDE THEM.

00:00:20.775 --> 00:00:22.784
JOINING US NOW, MARK PARKINSON,

00:00:22.785 --> 00:00:24.815
THE HEAD OF THE NATION’S LARGEST

00:00:24.816 --> 00:00:26.679
ASSOCIATIONS OF NURSING HOMES

00:00:26.713 --> 00:00:29.164
AND LONG-TERM CARE FACILITIES.

00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:30.289
MR. PARKINSON, A

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.229
"NEW YORK TIMES" STUDY FOUND

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:33.938
THAT ONE-THIRD, MORE THAN A

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:36.885
THIRD, OF ALL THE DEATHS IN THIS

00:00:36.887 --> 00:00:38.499
COUNTRY FROM COVID-19 HAVE BEEN

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:41.701
IN NURSING HOMES AND LONG-TERM

00:00:41.703 --> 00:00:42.342
CARE FACILITIES.

00:00:42.343 --> 00:00:46.184
OBVIOUSLY THE ELDERLY ARE AN

00:00:46.219 --> 00:00:47.524
ESPECIALLY VULNERABLE POPULATION

00:00:47.525 --> 00:00:47.844
POPULATION.

00:00:47.878 --> 00:00:48.990
INCIDENTALLY THIS WASN’T JUST

00:00:49.024 --> 00:00:50.445
PATIENTS, THIS WAS ALSO SOME OF

00:00:50.446 --> 00:00:51.846
THE WORKERS AT THE NURSING

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:52.990
HOMES, BUT WHY BE ON THAT

00:00:52.991 --> 00:00:54.343
VULNERABILITY, WHY DO YOU THINK

00:00:54.345 --> 00:00:56.553
SUCH A HIGH PERCENTAGE OF ALL

00:00:56.554 --> 00:00:57.942
THE DEATHS HAVE BEEN IN THESE

00:00:57.943 --> 00:00:58.347
FACILITIES?

00:00:58.348 --> 00:00:59.537
&gt;&gt; Mark: WELL, CHRIS, YOU’RE

00:00:59.572 --> 00:00:59.977
RIGHT.

00:01:00.011 --> 00:01:01.306
THIS HAS BEEN A HORRIBLE TRAGEDY

00:01:01.307 --> 00:01:03.143
AND FOR THOSE OF US THAT TAKE

00:01:03.145 --> 00:01:05.183
CARE OF OLDER PEOPLE OUR ENTIRE

00:01:05.184 --> 00:01:06.805
LIFE, IT’S BEEN THE MOST

00:01:06.806 --> 00:01:07.056
UNSPEAKABLE.

00:01:07.091 --> 00:01:08.999
WHAT WAS LEARNED FROM LOOKING

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.193
AROUND THE WORLD IS THAT

00:01:10.194 --> 00:01:13.015
ANYPLACE PEOPLE LIVE CLOSELY

00:01:13.017 --> 00:01:14.091
TOGETHER, WHETHER IT’S

00:01:14.126 --> 00:01:16.352
CONFIDENCE OR DORMITORIES OR

00:01:16.353 --> 00:01:18.450
CRUISE SHIPS OR NURSING HOMES,

00:01:18.451 --> 00:01:19.615
THEY’RE PARTICULARLY VULNERABLE

00:01:19.617 --> 00:01:21.382
AND IT’S BECAUSE OF ONE VERY

00:01:21.417 --> 00:01:23.006
UNIQUE FEATURE TO THIS VIRUS AND

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.937
THAT IS THAT THIS VIRUS, UNLIKE

00:01:24.938 --> 00:01:27.421
ANY OTHER THAT WE FOUGHT BEFORE,

00:01:27.455 --> 00:01:29.904
A PERSON CAN CATCH IT, SHOW NO

00:01:29.905 --> 00:01:31.964
SYMPTOMS YET STILL SPREAD IT.

00:01:31.965 --> 00:01:33.337
SO WHEN JANUARY FEBRUARY AND

00:01:33.371 --> 00:01:36.133
MARCH, WE DIDN’T KNOW THAT, WE

00:01:36.167 --> 00:01:37.999
HAVE VISITORS COMING INTO OUR

00:01:38.034 --> 00:01:39.438
BUILDINGS, WE HAD STAFF MEMBERS

00:01:39.439 --> 00:01:40.146
INTO BUILDINGS CLOSELY INTERACT

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:42.541
WITH RESIDENTS AS THEY NEED TO

00:01:42.575 --> 00:01:44.231
TAKE CARE OF THEM AND WE WERE

00:01:44.233 --> 00:01:45.814
UNWITTINGLY SPREADING THE VIRUS

00:01:45.815 --> 00:01:46.683
WITHIN THE COMMUNITIES.

00:01:46.684 --> 00:01:48.356
ONCE THE ACADEMIC COMMUNITY AND

00:01:48.391 --> 00:01:49.726
DOCTORS FIGURED OUT THAT YOU

00:01:49.727 --> 00:01:51.386
COULD BE ASYMPTOMATIC AND CARRY

00:01:51.421 --> 00:01:53.215
IT, IT WAS TOO LATE FOR A LOT OF

00:01:53.216 --> 00:01:54.104
PEOPLE AND UNFORTUNATELY EVEN

00:01:54.105 --> 00:01:55.857
THEN WE DIDN’T HAVE THE TESTS TO

00:01:55.859 --> 00:01:57.002
FIGURE OUT WHO HAD IT.

00:01:57.004 --> 00:01:58.664
THE GOOD IS THAT I CAN GIVE THIS

00:01:58.665 --> 00:02:00.204
MORNING AS WE ARE NOW IN

00:02:00.238 --> 00:02:01.593
RECOVERY -- I JUST WANT TO POINT

00:02:01.627 --> 00:02:03.748
OUT THAT THE TRUMP

00:02:03.782 --> 00:02:06.090
ADMINISTRATION JUST ON FRIDAY

00:02:06.124 --> 00:02:07.772
ALLOCATED $5 BILLION, SECRETARY

00:02:07.773 --> 00:02:09.501
AZAR, DEPUTY SECRETARY HARKIN,

00:02:09.502 --> 00:02:11.773
THAT’S GOING TO ALLOW US TO

00:02:11.808 --> 00:02:12.980
RECOVER AND REALLY MAKE THIS

00:02:13.014 --> 00:02:13.299
BETTER.

00:02:13.301 --> 00:02:15.526
&gt;&gt; Chris: I WANT TO POINT OUT

00:02:15.527 --> 00:02:18.455
ANOTHER ISSUE HOWEVER.

00:02:18.456 --> 00:02:19.991
THE GOVERNMENT ACCOUNT ABILITY

00:02:19.992 --> 00:02:21.142
OFFICE ISSUED A REPORT THIS WEEK

00:02:21.143 --> 00:02:23.076
AND I WANT TO PUT THE NUMBERS UP

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:24.506
ON THE SCREEN.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:28.128
IF FOUND -- IT FOUND THAT 82% OF

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:30.656
NURSING HOMES, OVER 13,000, HAVE

00:02:30.657 --> 00:02:34.657
BEEN CITED FOR INFECTION CONTROL

00:02:34.658 --> 00:02:37.770
ISSUES FROM 2013 TO 2017.

00:02:37.771 --> 00:02:39.287
SO THE QUESTION, MR. PARKINSON,

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:41.071
DIDIER FACILITIES HAVE A PROBLEM

00:02:41.072 --> 00:02:44.067
IN THIS PARTICULAR AREA LONG

00:02:44.069 --> 00:02:45.216
BEFORE THE PANDEMIC HIT?

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:47.262
&gt;&gt; Mr. Parkinson: WELL, WE

00:02:47.263 --> 00:02:48.657
HAVE A REAL FLAWED SURVEY SYSTEM

00:02:48.658 --> 00:02:50.928
AND ONE OF THE FLAWS OF THE

00:02:50.929 --> 00:02:52.094
SURVEY SYSTEM IS THAT SURVEYORS

00:02:52.129 --> 00:02:53.169
ARE ENCOURAGED TO GIVE

00:02:53.204 --> 00:02:54.251
DEFICIENCIES AND WHAT THAT DOES,

00:02:54.253 --> 00:02:55.455
IT CREATES THE IMPRESSION THAT

00:02:55.456 --> 00:02:57.099
EVEN VERY GOOD BUILDINGS ARE NOT

00:02:57.134 --> 00:02:57.811
VERY GOOD.

00:02:57.813 --> 00:02:59.258
IT MAKES IT HARD FOR CONSUMERS

00:02:59.259 --> 00:03:00.993
TO FIGURE OUT WHAT BUILDINGS ARE

00:03:01.028 --> 00:03:03.737
GOOD AND WHICH AREN’T EVERYBODY

00:03:03.771 --> 00:03:04.766
GETS DEFICIENCIES.

00:03:04.801 --> 00:03:07.238
THAT SAME GAO REPORT REPORTED

00:03:07.239 --> 00:03:09.251
THAT 99% OF THOSE DEFICIENCIES

00:03:09.252 --> 00:03:11.671
WERE NOT SEVERE, THEY DID NOT

00:03:11.706 --> 00:03:13.287
AFFECT PATIENT SAFETY AND MANY

00:03:13.289 --> 00:03:14.326
OF THEM WERE JUST PAPERWORK

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.113
ISSUES.

00:03:15.114 --> 00:03:17.560
THE REALITY IS THAT THE

00:03:17.594 --> 00:03:18.946
CORONAVIRUS VIOLATES ALL OF THE

00:03:18.947 --> 00:03:21.763
NORMAL CONCEPT CONCEPTIONS OF

00:03:21.797 --> 00:03:23.180
CONTROL BECAUSE NORMAL INFECTION

00:03:23.181 --> 00:03:24.617
CONTROL IS SYMPTOM RELATED.

00:03:24.618 --> 00:03:26.084
NOW THAT WE KNOW THAT WE ARE

00:03:26.085 --> 00:03:27.642
ADJUSTING OUR BEHAVIOR THAT IS

00:03:27.643 --> 00:03:29.305
WHERE WE ARE STARTING TO SEE

00:03:29.339 --> 00:03:30.463
RECOVERY AND PEOPLE ARE GETTING

00:03:30.497 --> 00:03:30.787
BETTER.

00:03:30.788 --> 00:03:32.783
VISITORS ARE NO LONGER ALLOWED

00:03:32.784 --> 00:03:34.995
TO COME INTO BUILDING.

00:03:35.029 --> 00:03:37.575
EVERY INTERACTION PATIENTS AND

00:03:37.609 --> 00:03:39.546
STAFF AND I HAVE ON.

00:03:39.548 --> 00:03:40.434
PATIENTS, RESIDENTS ARE NOT

00:03:40.435 --> 00:03:42.203
EATING TOGETHER IN THE SAME

00:03:42.238 --> 00:03:43.164
ROOM, THEY’RE EATING PRIVATELY

00:03:43.166 --> 00:03:44.521
IN OUR OWN ROOM SO NOW THAT WE

00:03:44.555 --> 00:03:45.751
UNDERSTAND THE VERY VICIOUS

00:03:45.786 --> 00:03:49.446
NATURE OF THE VIRUS, WE ARE ABLE

00:03:49.481 --> 00:03:50.904
TO CONTROL IT MUCH BETTER.

00:03:50.939 --> 00:03:53.362
&gt;&gt; Chris: NURSING HOMES IN

00:03:53.363 --> 00:03:55.698
NEW YORK AND NEW JERSEY HAVE

00:03:55.733 --> 00:03:58.279
BEEN ESPECIALLY HARD-HIT BY THE

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:00.772
PANDEMIC AS WELL AS THE ENTIRE

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:02.131
STATE AND IN LATE MARCH,

00:04:02.132 --> 00:04:05.677
GOVERNOR CUOMO ISSUED AN ORDER

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:08.794
THAT NURSING HOMES MUST ACCEPT

00:04:08.795 --> 00:04:10.601
COVID-19 PATIENTS TO TRY TO

00:04:10.635 --> 00:04:11.636
ALLEVIATE AND PREVENT

00:04:11.637 --> 00:04:13.468
OVERCROWDING AT HOSPITALS.

00:04:13.503 --> 00:04:14.890
HERE’S HOW THE GOVERNOR

00:04:14.891 --> 00:04:18.027
DESCRIBED IT AND EXPLAINED IT

00:04:18.061 --> 00:04:19.567
THIS WEEK.

00:04:19.569 --> 00:04:22.625
&gt;&gt; THE CDC GUIDANCE SET A HOMES

00:04:22.659 --> 00:04:23.648
CANNOT DISCRIMINATE AGAINST A

00:04:23.649 --> 00:04:26.251
COVID PATIENT BECAUSE AT THAT

00:04:26.286 --> 00:04:27.767
TIME THE ISSUE WAS HOSPITAL

00:04:27.768 --> 00:04:29.351
CAPACITY, RIGHT?

00:04:29.385 --> 00:04:30.618
REMEMBER HOSPITAL CAPACITY?

00:04:30.619 --> 00:04:33.197
AND WE WERE DRAMATICALLY

00:04:33.231 --> 00:04:35.387
INCREASING HOSPITAL CAPACITY.

00:04:35.422 --> 00:04:38.317
&gt;&gt; Chris: DID GOVERNOR CUOMO

00:04:38.351 --> 00:04:41.318
HAVE TO FOLLOW THAT CDC

00:04:41.352 --> 00:04:42.829
GUIDANCE, OR GPU OBITUARIES?

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:43.853
AND WHAT ABOUT OTHER GOVERNORS

00:04:43.887 --> 00:04:46.055
AND HOW THEY HANDLE THE CDC

00:04:46.056 --> 00:04:47.267
GUIDANCE ON THE COUNTRY?

00:04:47.301 --> 00:04:48.573
&gt;&gt; Mr. Parkinson: LOOK, I’VE

00:04:48.574 --> 00:04:50.790
BEEN A GOVERNOR IN THE TIME OF A

00:04:50.824 --> 00:04:52.377
CRISIS, SO I UNDERSTAND THAT

00:04:52.411 --> 00:04:53.591
SOMETIMES YOU HAVE TO MAKE A

00:04:53.625 --> 00:04:55.996
DECISION BASED ON INCOMPLETE

00:04:55.998 --> 00:04:57.928
INFORMATION AND THE TIME THAT

00:04:57.929 --> 00:04:59.075
GOVERNOR CUOMO MADE THAT

00:04:59.109 --> 00:05:00.778
DECISION HE WAS BEING TOLD A

00:05:00.812 --> 00:05:01.392
EPIDEMIOLOGIST THAT HAS

00:05:01.393 --> 00:05:02.616
HOSPITALS WERE GOING TO BE

00:05:02.617 --> 00:05:03.639
OVERRUN WITH COVID PATIENTS.

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:05.735
IN HINDSIGHT WE NOW KNOW THAT

00:05:05.737 --> 00:05:07.408
THAT WAS NOT THE CASE.

00:05:07.442 --> 00:05:08.911
THERE WAS ACTUALLY THE CAPACITY

00:05:08.945 --> 00:05:11.889
THERE, THEY DIDN’T NEED TO BE

00:05:11.923 --> 00:05:13.100
DISCHARGED TO NURSING HOMES.

00:05:13.101 --> 00:05:14.500
IN HINDSIGHT, IT WAS AN ERROR

00:05:14.502 --> 00:05:17.854
APPEARED IN TO HIS CREDIT HE HAS

00:05:17.888 --> 00:05:18.921
NO REVERSE THAT POLICY.

00:05:18.956 --> 00:05:19.789
MOST OF THE OTHER GOVERNORS

00:05:19.823 --> 00:05:21.057
ACROSS THE COUNTRY TO NOT

00:05:21.091 --> 00:05:22.362
INSTITUTE THAT POLICY AND I

00:05:22.363 --> 00:05:25.209
THINK THAT’S PART OF THE REASON

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:26.319
WE’RE STARTING TO SEE RECOVERY.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:28.058
&gt;&gt; Chris: BUT IN FACT HE DID

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:28.766
HAVE A CHOICE.

00:05:28.801 --> 00:05:31.597
HE DIDN’T HAVE TO FOLLOW THE CDC

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:32.753
GUIDANCE ANYWAY.

00:05:32.754 --> 00:05:34.322
&gt;&gt; I MEAN, IN HINDSIGHT ARE

00:05:34.324 --> 00:05:36.103
SUGGESTED TO HIM AT THE TIME WAS

00:05:36.105 --> 00:05:37.877
THAT HE DIDN’T DO THAT.

00:05:37.878 --> 00:05:39.699
I THINK IN HINDSIGHT HE WOULD

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:41.307
SAY THAT IT WAS AN ERROR.

00:05:41.308 --> 00:05:43.453
IT WAS AN ERROR AGAIN BASED ON

00:05:43.454 --> 00:05:44.300
INCOMPLETE AND INACCURATE

00:05:44.334 --> 00:05:44.819
INFORMATION.

00:05:44.854 --> 00:05:48.097
THE COUNTRY WAS TOO CONCERNED

00:05:48.098 --> 00:05:50.068
WITH HOSPITALS BEING OVERRUN AND

00:05:50.069 --> 00:05:52.853
THERE WERE CONSEQUENCES TO THAT.

00:05:52.854 --> 00:05:55.092
ONE OF THE CONSEQUENCES IS THAT

00:05:55.094 --> 00:05:56.115
NURSING HOMES WERE LEFT OUT.

00:05:56.116 --> 00:05:57.648
IF WE WEREN’T GIVEN THE

00:05:57.649 --> 00:05:58.499
EQUIPMENT THAT WE NEEDED.

00:05:58.533 --> 00:06:00.075
THERE NEEDS TO BE SOME ACCOUNT

00:06:00.077 --> 00:06:02.186
ABILITY FOR ALL OF THESE PEOPLE

00:06:02.187 --> 00:06:03.672
THAT WERE MAKING THESE FANTASTIC

00:06:03.674 --> 00:06:04.514
ESTIMATES THAT THE ENTIRE

00:06:04.548 --> 00:06:06.084
HOSPITAL SYSTEM ACROSS THE

00:06:06.085 --> 00:06:08.607
COUNTRY WAS GOING TO BE OVERRUN.

00:06:08.642 --> 00:06:09.966
IT WASN’T, AND THERE ARE

00:06:09.967 --> 00:06:10.703
CONSEQUENCES AND UNFORTUNATELY

00:06:10.738 --> 00:06:13.142
NURSING HOME RESIDENTS OR ONE OF

00:06:13.143 --> 00:06:13.887
THE CONSEQUENCES.

00:06:13.889 --> 00:06:15.472
&gt;&gt; Chris: I WANT TO PICK UP ON

00:06:15.507 --> 00:06:17.794
THE FIRST POINT YOU MADE, WHICH

00:06:17.829 --> 00:06:21.088
IS THAT WE DIDN’T KNOW AT THE

00:06:21.089 --> 00:06:23.087
VERY BEGINNING A LOT OF THE

00:06:23.088 --> 00:06:23.907
PARTICULARLY TERRIFYING AND

00:06:23.908 --> 00:06:25.254
DANGEROUS ASPECTS OF THE

00:06:25.289 --> 00:06:27.507
CORONAVIRUS, AND ONE OF THEM IS

00:06:27.541 --> 00:06:29.357
THAT PEOPLE COULD BE

00:06:29.359 --> 00:06:31.439
ASYMPTOMATIC AND GO INTO A

00:06:31.473 --> 00:06:33.434
HOSPITAL WITHOUT ANY SIGN THEIR

00:06:33.468 --> 00:06:36.022
ILL AND THEN STILL SPREAD THE

00:06:36.056 --> 00:06:38.075
VIRUS THESE VERY SICK PEOPLE.

00:06:38.076 --> 00:06:40.361
THE RESULT, AS YOU’VE LOCKED

00:06:40.363 --> 00:06:42.325
DOWN, IS WE’VE SEEN THESE

00:06:42.326 --> 00:06:43.847
TERRIBLE SCENES WHERE FOR THEIR

00:06:43.848 --> 00:06:45.761
OWN GOOD, RESIDENTS ARE KEPT

00:06:45.763 --> 00:06:47.731
AWAY FROM THEIR FAMILIES AT SOME

00:06:47.765 --> 00:06:49.052
OF THEM GET VERY SICK, SOME OF

00:06:49.054 --> 00:06:50.466
THEM PASS AWAY AND THEIR

00:06:50.467 --> 00:06:53.076
FAMILIES CAN’T BE WITH THEM WHEN

00:06:53.111 --> 00:06:53.687
THAT HAPPENS.

00:06:53.722 --> 00:06:56.578
WHAT ARE YOUR THOUGHTS ABOUT

00:06:56.579 --> 00:06:58.698
REOPENING NURSING HOMES, LETTING

00:06:58.699 --> 00:07:02.429
FAMILIES BE WITH THE RESIDENTS

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:04.751
AND UNDER WHAT STRUCTURES, UNDER

00:07:04.786 --> 00:07:06.070
WHAT RESTRICTION SO THAT THE

00:07:06.072 --> 00:07:07.000
FAMILIES CAN BE TOGETHER BUT

00:07:07.034 --> 00:07:09.534
YOU’RE NOT ENDANGERING THE LIVES

00:07:09.535 --> 00:07:11.288
OF ALL THE PATIENTS INSIDE THESE

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:11.521
FACILITIES?

00:07:11.522 --> 00:07:12.769
&gt;&gt; Mr. Parkinson: WE REALIZE

00:07:12.803 --> 00:07:15.216
HOW HARD IT’S BEEN FOR FAMILY

00:07:15.217 --> 00:07:16.600
MEMBERS AND FOR RESIDENTS TO NOT

00:07:16.634 --> 00:07:18.640
BE ABLE TO BE TOGETHER AND WE

00:07:18.641 --> 00:07:20.781
TRY TO OFFER FACE TIME AND ALL

00:07:20.782 --> 00:07:22.347
SORTS OF OTHER ALTERNATIVES, BUT

00:07:22.381 --> 00:07:23.903
THERE’S JUST NO ALTERNATIVE TO

00:07:23.938 --> 00:07:25.145
BEING TOGETHER AND THEN THE

00:07:25.146 --> 00:07:27.750
TRAGIC SCENES OF PEOPLE DYING

00:07:27.751 --> 00:07:29.571
WITHOUT THEIR LOVED ONES, IT’S

00:07:29.572 --> 00:07:29.808
HORRIBLE.

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:31.324
THE MOST IMPORTANT THING IS THAT

00:07:31.358 --> 00:07:32.924
WE NEED TO KEEP THE 15 DOWN IN

00:07:32.958 --> 00:07:35.336
THE COMMUNITIES THAT THE NURSING

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:36.440
HOMES ARE IN.

00:07:36.475 --> 00:07:38.135
IF A NURSING HOME IS IN A

00:07:38.137 --> 00:07:39.069
COMMUNITY THAT HAS VERY LITTLE

00:07:39.071 --> 00:07:41.178
COVID THERE’S NOT THAT HUGE RISK

00:07:41.179 --> 00:07:42.675
OF A GETTING TO THE BUILDINGS.

00:07:42.709 --> 00:07:44.561
IF WE SPIKED BACK UP AND COVID

00:07:44.562 --> 00:07:46.234
CASES THOUGH, WE’RE GOING TO END

00:07:46.235 --> 00:07:47.714
UP WITH MORE COVID IN NURSING

00:07:47.749 --> 00:07:48.016
HOMES.

00:07:48.051 --> 00:07:50.951
ISSUE ONE IS LET’S KEEP IT DOWN

00:07:50.986 --> 00:07:52.446
THE COMMUNITIES AND LET STEP TWO

00:07:52.447 --> 00:07:53.844
IS LET’S GET ADEQUATE TESTING SO

00:07:53.878 --> 00:07:56.032
WE CAN GET A TEST FOR EVERY

00:07:56.067 --> 00:07:57.180
STAFF MEMBER, EVERY RESIDENT AND

00:07:57.181 --> 00:07:58.426
IDEAL IF WE COULD GET ON-SITE

00:07:58.427 --> 00:07:59.895
TESTING FELT THE SUMMER SO THAT

00:07:59.896 --> 00:08:01.849
WHEN PEOPLE COME AND THEY GET A

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:04.678
TEST, WE KNOW THAT THEY ARE

00:08:04.679 --> 00:08:06.561
COVID-FREE, THAT WOULD BE THE

00:08:06.562 --> 00:08:08.197
IDEAL, BUT WE DO RECOGNIZE IT’S

00:08:08.232 --> 00:08:11.019
EXTREMELY IMPORTANT TO GET THESE

00:08:11.053 --> 00:08:12.646
FOLKS BACK WITH THEIR FAMILIES.

00:08:12.681 --> 00:08:13.478
&gt;&gt; Chris: MR. PARKINSON,

00:08:13.479 --> 00:08:14.198
THANK YOU, THANKS FOR TAKING

